  "solution": "Given:\n\n(8, 388, 18)\n\n(11, 137, 4)\n\n**Logic:** Second no. = [(First no.)² +(Third no.)²]\n\n(8, 388, 18) →\n\n⇒ [(8)² + (18)²]\n\n⇒ (64 + 324) = 388\n\n(11, 137, 4) →\n\n⇒ [(11)2 + (4)2]\n\n⇒ (121 + 16) = 137\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n1. (15, 230, 2) →\n\n⇒ [(15)2 + (2)2]\n\n⇒ (225 + 4) = 229\n\n2. (3, 51, 7) →\n\n⇒ [(3)2 + (7)2]\n\n⇒ (9 + 49) = 58\n\n3. (10, 118, 9) →\n\n⇒ [(10)2 + (9)2]\n\n⇒ (100 + 81) = 181\n\n**4. (14, 221, 5) →**\n\n⇒ [(14)2 + (5)2]\n\n⇒ (196 + 25) = **221**\n\nHere, **(14, 221, 5)** shows a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (4)\".",
